          dealing: 'Initial Deal: 3 cards to each player, 4 cards face-up to table\nSubsequent Deals: 3 cards each when hands are empty (no more table cards)\nDealing Pattern: Counterclockwise\nDirection: Counterclockwise play',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Score points by capturing cards from the table (making combinations that sum to 15) and declaring special three-card combinations in hand. The game is played to an agreed target score (commonly 21 or 31 points).',
          gameplay: '1. First dealer chosen randomly, deals 3 cards to each player and 4 to table\n2. If 2+ Aces on table, reshuffle and redeal\n3. Players take turns counterclockwise\n4. On turn: Play one card to capture cards summing to 15 (including by matching a single 15-value card, or making combinations that sum to 15)\n5. If capture made: Take captured cards and played card, store as trick\n6. If no capture: Played card stays on table\n7. After all play their 3 cards, dealer deals 3 more to each player\n8. Continue until all cards played\n9. Last player to capture takes remaining table cards\n10. Score points based on captured cards and declarations',
          keyRules: [
            'Captures must sum to exactly 15',
            'A single card can capture if it matches a table card of same value',
            "Multiple table cards can be captured if they sum to the played card's value",
            'Escoba (sweep): Capturing all table cards at once - worth 1 point',
            'Declaration bonuses are announced before playing, with specific procedures',
            'Wild cards may be used in some variants (e.g., 7 of cups)',
            "If dealer's initial 4 table cards sum to 15, dealer captures them for bonus",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Focus on capturing cards that sum to 15. Try to capture the settebello (7 of coins) and accumulate sevens. Watch for opportunities to make an escoba (sweep).',
          intermediate: 'Count cards to track what values remain. Set up escoba opportunities by leaving specific card combinations on the table. Declare bonuses when you have qualifying combinations in hand.',
          advanced: 'Complex probability calculations for capture opportunities. Strategic use of declaration bonuses. Control table state to limit opponent escoba chances while maximizing your own. Track suit distribution for primiera and coins majority.',
          tips: [
            'The 7 of coins (settebello) is crucial - prioritize capturing it',
            'Setting up an escoba can provide a significant swing',
            'Declaration bonuses can add substantial points - learn the combinations',
            'Track which cards have been played to predict remaining captures',
            "Sometimes playing a card that doesn't capture can set up future plays",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
